WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
In January, Coober Pedy averages 28.3
megajoules of solar exposure per square

2
00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.890
metre every day.

3
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:13.070
In Morocco, the Noor-Ouarzazate complex
was planned to turn desert sun into 500

4
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.770
megawatts of power.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.370
And a 2019 study counted
15,906 desalination plants,

6
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.270
producing about 95 million cubic
metres of fresh water daily.

7
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.750
Sun and seawater: can technology turn
them into reliable power and water?

8
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.330
Cheaply, with no side effects?

9
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:38.850
In this mission, you'll follow Noor-Ouarzazate
from its first 160 megawatt phase.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.290
Then you'll judge desalination and desert
solar against a test of sustainable

11
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.630
development.

12
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.430
Your mission: evaluate whether solar power
and desalination can make desert living

13
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.480
sustainable.
